============================================================
        TESTNG ISSUE — "Instantiating tests..." STUCK
============================================================

ISSUE:
------
TestNG was getting stuck at:

    Instantiating tests...

Reason:
-------
I created an object of the SAME TestNG class inside the class:

    Test002_Post ts = new Test002_Post();


WHY THIS CAUSES THE PROBLEM:
----------------------------

When Java creates a Test002_Post object:

    new Test002_Post()
            ↓
    Class initialization starts
            ↓
    Test002_Post ts = new Test002_Post()
            ↓
    Creates another Test002_Post object
            ↓
    Again creates another Test002_Post object
            ↓
    Again...
            ↓
           ∞


This causes RECURSIVE OBJECT CREATION.


TESTNG FLOW:
------------

TestNG
   ↓
Creates Test002_Post object
   ↓
Initializes class variables
   ↓
Finds @Test method
   ↓
Executes m1()


But because of:

    Test002_Post ts = new Test002_Post();

the object creation keeps repeating.


WRONG:
------

public class Test002_Post {

    Test002_Post ts = new Test002_Post();

    @Test
    public void m1() {
        // test code
    }
}


CORRECT:
--------

public class Test002_Post {

    @Test
    public void m1() {
        // test code
    }
}


IMPORTANT:
----------

TestNG automatically creates the object of the test class.

We DON'T need to manually create:

    Test002_Post ts = new Test002_Post();


KEY POINT TO REMEMBER:
----------------------

For a TestNG test class:

    TestNG → Creates Object → Finds @Test → Executes Test


If we create the same class object inside itself:

    new Test002_Post()
            ↓
    new Test002_Post()
            ↓
    new Test002_Post()
            ↓
    ...

This can cause the test execution to get stuck at:

    "Instantiating tests..."


INTERVIEW POINT:
----------------

Question:
Why should we not create an object of the TestNG test class
inside itself?

Answer:
TestNG automatically creates the test class instance.
Creating another instance of the same class during its own
initialization causes recursive object creation and can prevent
TestNG from completing test instantiation.


REMEMBER:
---------

❌ Don't do:

    Test002_Post ts = new Test002_Post();


✅ Do:

    public class Test002_Post {

        @Test
        public void m1() {
            // test code
        }
    }

